Z||000000||Black88GT||06-10-2001||03:38 PM||||I went to see this movie the other night.  I thought it was pretty damn good.  The first hour was kind of boring with all the love stuff, but it was worth sitting through just to see the next 2 hours.  It was like "Days of our Lives" meets "Saving Private Ryan" in a way.  <P>I never listen to critics because they usually can't tell a good movie if it hit them on the head.  They proved me right again as I found out they gave the movie a one out of five.  A one??  Are you kidding me?? This movie was 100 times better then "Titanic", and much much more educational.  I swear you almost felt like you were living during that era, they did such a good job of going through all the steps and everything that led up to the attack.<P>Anyone else?<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://88database.homestead.com/files/AF.gif">     <BR><I>"Once you go black, you never go back..."</I><BR><I>"The Customer Can Have Any Color He Wants So Long As It's Black" </I> -Henry Ford||||reg||14
