Z||000005||onfire||06-11-2001||02:18 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLisa:<BR><B>Went to see Moulin Rouge the other night, it was certainly....different....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, but it was still a pretty good movie. When that one guy with the deep voice started singing Roxanne that was awesome. And all those other songs, if you like music go see it.<P>If you wanna see a funny movie go see The Animal. I have yet to see Pearl Harbour. Swordfish was a good action movie.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||06-11-2001||03:49 AM||||I want to see Swordfish.. but the one I'm waiting for is The Fast and The Furious.... not quite as catchy a title as Gone in 60 Seconds though.. (love that movie. seen it 3 times this week already in fact.. my sister had it on, and each time I'd just sit down and watch it with her, or watch a few minutes whenever I was in the room)<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||10
Z||000007||poupas||06-11-2001||05:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I went to see this movie the other night.  I thought it was pretty damn good.  The first hour was kind of boring with all the love stuff, but it was worth sitting through just to see the next 2 <BR>Anyone else?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>  Yea, I saw Pearl Harbour, this is my review. It is a three hour movie, two hours are a complete waste of time with a love triangle, the other hour is AMAZING. Incredible special effects. I would recommend going to see this movie 1.5 hours after it starts and you will enjoy it as much as everyone else that has been sitting there twice as long. The fight scene is ranked as one of the best ever( in my book).<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cliff Pennock||12-08-2001||06:47 PM||||Sorry to dig up this old post but I just saw Pearl Harbour on DVD and I thought it was a <B>very</B> good movie. The only thing I didn't like was that they did the "Titanic-trick": start the film with some 1.5 hour long romantic moosh so women will like it immediately (sorry if that offends anyone), than switch to one hour of heavy action so the men will wake up and think it's a great flick, then end the movie with a romantic note so it will stick in women's minds (and because it follows the action, men will forget that).<BR>||||reg||1
